      "problem": "Solve for $k$ where $\\frac{5k+2}{3}=\\frac{3}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5k+2}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ (5k+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5k+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (3) \\\\ 10k+4 & =9 \\\\ 10k+4-4 & =9-4 \\\\ 10k & =5 \\\\ \\frac{10k}{10} & =\\frac{5}{10} \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
